## Group Workstations

A workstation is a dedicated server allocated with CPU, memory, and disk storage
resources. Projects are run on workstations and share the resources of the
workstation.

Note: "workstations" are known as "hosts" internally at Nitrous, hence the
endpoint names and response envelopes.

### Create a New Workstation [POST /hosts]

You can create a workstation for either your account or for your users - just
use the appropriate Bearer token.

Your request will be accepted immediately, and the workstation will be created
asynchronously. Creating a workstation usually takes between 20 seconds to 3
minutes.

Use the `/hosts/{slug}` endpoint to determine when a workstation has been
created. Its state (initially `born`) will be `running` when it's been
created successfully.

+ Request

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN

    + Attributes
        + name (required, string) - Workstation name. Spaces are allowed.
        + region (required, string) - Slug of the workstation's region.
        + org (optional, string) - Org slug. The workstation created will belong to this organization.
        + size (optional, string) - Slug of the workstation's plan. If not specified, `org` is required
        + async (required, boolean) - Always this to `true`, for now

+ Response 202 (application/json)
    + Body

            {
                "host": {
                    "id": 18,
                    "user_id": 14,
                    "region_id": 8,
                    "plan_id": 21,
                    "org_id": 1,
                    "slug": "my-ws-1293",
                    "name": "My WS",
                    "ip_address": "",
                    "hostname": "my-ws-1293.nitrouspro.com",
                    "proxy_hostname": "my-ws-1293.nitrouspro.com",
                    "size": "org-plus",
                    "state": "born",
                    "created_at": "2016-03-01T04:32:54.844284Z",
                    "updated_at": "2016-03-01T04:32:54.844284Z",
                    "auto_shutdown": false,
                    "max_containers": 20
                    "shared": false
                }
            }

### Show a Workstation's Info [GET /hosts/{slug}]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string) ... Slug identifying the workstation.

+ Request

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body

            {
                "host": {
                    "id": 18,
                    "user_id": 14,
                    "region_id": 8,
                    "plan_id": 21,
                    "org_id": 1,
                    "slug": "my-ws-1293",
