## Group Projects

A project is the most common unit that users interact with. Users connect to
their project to edit code, run servers, and preview their application. Each
project runs in its own isolated environment, distinct from other projects.

Note: "projects" are known as "containers" internally at Nitrous, hence the
endpoint names and response envelopes.

### Creating a New Project [POST /containers/create_atomic]

Creating a project requires a `running` workstation.

Your request will be accepted immediately, and the project will be created
asynchronously. Creating a project takes between 1 second to 2 minutes.

Use the `/containers/{slug}` endpoint to determine when a project has been
created. Its state (initially `created`) will be `running` when it's been
created successfully.

+ Request

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN

    + Attributes
        + host (required, string) - Slug of workstation that the new project should live in.
        + name (required, string) - Project name. Spaces are allowed.
        + template (optional, string) - Slug of template to create the project from. Either `template` or `snapshot_id` are required.
        + `snapshot_id` (optional, number) - ID of snapshot to create the project from. Either `template` or `snapshot_id` are required.

+ Response 202 (application/json)
    + Body

            {
                "container": {
                    "id": 8,
                    "cid": "",
                    "user_id": 1,
                    "host_id": 12,
                    "image": "quay.io/nitrous/ubuntu:latest",
                    "slug": "grandeur-firefly-100007",
                    "name": "Grandeur Firefly",
                    "state": "unknown",
                    "preview_hostname": "grandeur-firefly-100007.nitrousapp.com",
                    "created_at": "2016-03-01T05:10:46.092807Z",
                    "updated_at": "2016-03-01T05:10:46.092807Z"
                },
                "request_id": "bf1258ca"
            }

### Show a Project's Info [GET /containers/{slug}]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string) ... Slug identifying the project.

+ Request

    + Headers

            Authorization: Bearer OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body

            {
                "container": {
                    "id": 9,
                    "cid": "67a26a67f6d3c6f7f50ee7d0957fabf148a3b1efb804fa44ea4d901ddd1f7495",
