## Group Collaborators

You can add other users as collaborators to a project to grant them access to
it. This will allow multiple users to work collaboratively on a single project
simultaneously.

You can also add a user as collaborator to a project on your workstation so that
you do not have to create a workstation for the user. This is useful when you do
want full control and accounting over the workstations, since they would be
under your Nitrous account.

### Adding Collaborator to a Project [POST /containers/{slug}/collaborators]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string) ... Slug identifying the project.

+ Request
    + Attributes
        + user (required, string) - Username of user to add as a collaborator to the project.
        + noemail (optional, string) - Set to `true` to suppress the Nitrous-branded email sent to the user notifying them that they have been added as a collaborator.

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Body

            {
                "success": true
            }

